            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "In 2015 the Internal Revenue Service notified Boechler, P.C., a North Dakota law firm, of a discrepancy in its tax filings."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Boechler, P.C.",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f376976326ff9e75be8cfa9da6cb7ed25f056b7e86514d3095aae710dc74d5e9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f376976326ff-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Boechler, P.C., according to Boechler, P.C., boechler challenged the penalty, arguing that there was no discrepancy and that the penalty was excessive."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Commissioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f376976326ff9e75be8cfa9da6cb7ed25f056b7e86514d3095aae710dc74d5e9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f376976326ff-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Commissioner, the Commissioner asserted that the missed deadline extinguished Boechler\u2019s opportunity to seek review because the deadline is jurisdictional, meaning the Tax Court lacks authority to consider late petitions."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Supreme Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f376976326ff9e75be8cfa9da6cb7ed25f056b7e86514d3095aae710dc74d5e9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f376976326ff-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Boechler filed its petition one day after the 30\u2011day deadline, missing the statutory window."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background and Question",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "case_id": "2021-20-1472",
  "decision": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f376976326ff9e75be8cfa9da6cb7ed25f056b7e86514d3095aae710dc74d5e9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f376976326ff-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 14,
              "start": 14
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that the 30\u2011day time limit in \u00a7\u202f6330(d)(1) is an ordinary, non\u2011jurisdictional deadline that is subject to equitable tolling."
      }
    ],
